// THE STATED FRONTIER, and a probe for it. A PAYLOAD-ABSENT arm (`Leaf`, `Absent`, `None`) is not a
// construct node at all: v2.std.node_query construct_tag_reading answers NotAConstruct for an atom, and
// the walk sends an atom to the qualified-name door. So the constructor-set reading cannot reach a nullary
// arm, and it stays unbound here exactly as it does on main. This claim asserts TODAY'S ANSWER on purpose;
// it is the discriminating control for the one extension this PR does NOT make -- reading a payload-absent
// atom through the same expected-type door. TRIGGER: that extension, which is a scope question for
// tidy-ant-251 (it widens the door from construct nodes to atoms) and would flip this claim to the arm
// binding. It is not a relabel: today the site refuses.
test fn a_payload_absent_arm_is_not_a_construct_node_and_stays_unbound() -> Bool {
  match ctee_verdicts() {
    Absent => false
    Present { value: vs } => ctee_refuses_with(v: vs.nullary, reason: ^resolve_reason_unbound_symbol)
  }
}

